<h2 id="who">Who is the Best Gynecologist in Ambikapur?</h2>
<p>The honest answer is that "best" depends on what you need. A woman with unexplained bleeding needs a good diagnostician. A woman in her 34th week carrying twins needs someone comfortable with high-risk obstetrics. A woman with a 7 cm fibroid needs a surgeon who can remove it without a large open cut.</p>
<p>Dr. Ankita Bansal Goyal covers all three. She completed her <strong>M.D. and FMAS at PGIMER Chandigarh</strong>, one of India's leading medical institutes, and has over 15 years of clinical practice in obstetrics, gynaecology and minimal access surgery. At Sankalp Hospital she works with <strong>Ambikapur's first and only 3D Rubina laser laparoscopic system</strong>, which adds depth perception and real-time fluorescence imaging during surgery. In practice that means smaller incisions, less blood loss and a faster return home.</p>
<p>When comparing doctors anywhere, check four things: qualification and surgical training, whether the same doctor sees you at every visit, whether the hospital can handle an emergency at 2 AM, and whether costs are explained <em>before</em> treatment starts rather than after.</p>

<h2 id="services">Services From First Period to Menopause</h2>
<p>Women's health is not only about pregnancy. The clinic handles the full range of gynaecological and obstetric care:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Pregnancy and antenatal care:</strong> booking visit, scans, blood tests, iron and folic acid supplementation, anaemia correction and diet planning.</li>
    <li><strong>Normal delivery and caesarean section:</strong> with continuous labour monitoring throughout.</li>
    <li><strong><a href="../high-risk-pregnancy-in-ambikapur.php" style="color:#ee7c31; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline;">High-risk pregnancy care</a>:</strong> diabetes in pregnancy, high blood pressure, twins, previous caesarean, thyroid disorders and low-lying placenta.</li>
    <li><strong><a href="../pcos-pcod-treatment-in-ambikapur.php" style="color:#ee7c31; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline;">PCOS and PCOD treatment</a>:</strong> irregular cycles, unwanted hair growth, weight gain and difficulty conceiving.</li>
    <li><strong><a href="../fibroid-treatment-in-ambikapur.php" style="color:#ee7c31; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline;">Fibroid treatment</a>:</strong> medical management and laparoscopic myomectomy that preserves the uterus.</li>
    <li><strong><a href="../ovarian-cyst-removal-in-ambikapur.php" style="color:#ee7c31; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline;">Ovarian cyst removal</a>:</strong> alongside <a href="../endometriosis-care.php" style="color:#ee7c31; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline;">specialised endometriosis care</a>.</li>
    <li><strong><a href="../gynecological-surgery-in-ambikapur.php" style="color:#ee7c31; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline;">Gynecological surgery</a>:</strong> including laparoscopic hysterectomy through keyhole incisions.</li>
    <li><strong>Infertility evaluation:</strong> tubal testing, ovulation tracking, and IVF referral only when genuinely indicated.</li>
    <li><strong>Menstrual and menopause care:</strong> heavy bleeding, painful periods, hot flushes and bone health.</li>
    <li><strong>Preventive care:</strong> Pap smear, HPV vaccination and adolescent gynaecology counselling.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="female">Is There a Female Gynecologist in Ambikapur?</h2>
<p>Yes. Dr. Ankita Bansal Goyal is a female gynecologist and obstetrician practising in Ambikapur. Many women, especially first-time patients and adolescent girls, feel more comfortable discussing periods, discharge, infertility or sexual health with a lady doctor. Every internal examination is carried out privately, with a female attendant present.</p>
<p>This matters more than people admit. Plenty of gynaecological problems in Surguja are diagnosed late simply because the patient waited months before speaking to anyone. If having a <strong>lady doctor in Ambikapur</strong> is what makes you come in earlier, that is reason enough.</p>

<h2 id="fees">Fees, Timings and Booking</h2>
<p>Private gynaecologist consultations in Ambikapur generally fall between &#8377;300 and &#8377;800, depending on whether it is a first visit or a follow-up. Scans, blood tests and procedures are billed separately, and the estimate is shared with you before anything begins. If surgery is advised, ask for the total package cost in writing. A good clinic will give it without hesitation.</p>
<p><strong>Booking takes three steps:</strong> call or WhatsApp <a href="tel:+919691212570" style="color:#ee7c31; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline;">096912 12570</a> with your name, age and main complaint; confirm a slot, which matters most if you are travelling in from outside Ambikapur; and carry your file, including previous prescriptions, scan films and old reports.</p>

<h2 id="pregnancy">Pregnancy Care and Scan Schedule</h2>
<p>Book your first visit as soon as a home pregnancy test is positive, ideally by 6 to 8 weeks. The first scan confirms the pregnancy is inside the uterus and shows the heartbeat. After that, visits are monthly until 28 weeks, every two weeks until 36 weeks, and weekly until delivery.</p>
<div class="dabg-table">
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>What Happens at This Visit</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>6 to 8 weeks</td><td>Booking visit, dating scan, blood group, haemoglobin, thyroid, sugar and infection screening</td></tr>
        <tr><td>11 to 13 weeks</td><td>NT scan and double marker test</td></tr>
        <tr><td>18 to 20 weeks</td><td>Anomaly scan, the detailed check of the baby's organs</td></tr>
        <tr><td>24 to 28 weeks</td><td>Glucose test for gestational diabetes, tetanus dose, iron and calcium review</td></tr>
        <tr><td>32 to 36 weeks</td><td>Growth scan, baby's position and Doppler study if needed</td></tr>
        <tr><td>37 weeks onwards</td><td>Weekly review, delivery planning and birth preparedness</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>Anaemia deserves a special mention. It is extremely common in this region and is one of the most preventable causes of complications during delivery. Iron and folic acid supplementation, started early and taken consistently, changes outcomes far more than most patients realise.</p>

<h2 id="delivery">Normal Delivery or Caesarean?</h2>
<p>Any hospital you choose for delivery should have three things available at all hours: a doctor who can perform an emergency caesarean, blood arrangement, and newborn care support. Ask about these directly. The answer tells you more than the size of the waiting room.</p>
<p>Normal delivery is always preferred when it is safe for mother and baby. What genuinely improves the chances is regular antenatal visits, controlled weight gain, correcting anaemia early, staying active through pregnancy, and monitoring the baby's position after 36 weeks. A caesarean is advised when there is a real medical reason such as foetal distress, obstructed labour, placenta praevia, a breech baby, or certain previous surgeries.</p>
<p>On cost, a normal delivery in a private setup in Ambikapur is usually considerably cheaper than a caesarean, since a caesarean adds theatre charges, anaesthesia and a longer stay. Government facilities cost less, while private care generally offers continuity with the same doctor from the first visit through to discharge. Either way, ask for a written estimate.</p>

<h2 id="pcos">PCOS and Irregular Periods</h2>
<p><strong>Can PCOS be treated without surgery?</strong> Yes, in most cases. PCOS is a hormonal and metabolic condition, so the foundation of treatment is lifestyle. Losing even 5 to 10 percent of body weight can restore ovulation on its own. Medicines are added to regularise cycles, improve insulin sensitivity, or induce ovulation when a woman is trying to conceive. Laparoscopic ovarian drilling is reserved for the small group who do not respond to medical treatment.</p>
<p><strong>What causes irregular periods after 30?</strong> The usual causes are PCOS, thyroid disorders, anaemia, fibroids or polyps, sudden weight change, and stress. After 40, perimenopause enters the picture. A pelvic ultrasound along with thyroid, haemoglobin and hormone tests usually identifies the reason within a single visit, which is why waiting a year for things to settle on their own rarely helps.</p>
<p><strong>Symptoms that should not wait:</strong> bleeding between periods, after intercourse or any bleeding after menopause; periods lasting more than seven days or soaking through protection every one to two hours; severe pelvic pain that stops you working or attending school; not conceiving after one year of trying, or six months if you are over 35; a breast lump or persistent foul-smelling discharge.</p>

