        {"@type":"Question","name":"How many weeks pregnant should I be for my first scan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The first scan is usually done between 6 and 8 weeks to confirm the pregnancy, its location and the heartbeat. The next important scan is the NT scan at 11 to 13 weeks, followed by the anomaly scan at 18 to 20 weeks and growth scans in the third trimester."}},
